ain eps ~ sqrt(x) / log^4 x need K = log^6 x zeros. **Distinction from S195/Thread 3**: S195 closed Thread 3 ("polylog K -> threshold hit-rate -> 0 -> exact pi(x) hopeless in polylog"); Thread 7 slot 1 RE-FRAMES the same variance formula to ask the complementary algorithmic question ("polylog K -> what is the smallest typical eps?") and gives a positive named-exponent answer. Two complementary results: threshold negative + quantitative positive. **Open vs A-grade gap**: result is heuristic (random-phase model unproven); single-sample-per-decade rather than 20+ samples; "polylog improvement" is log-factor not x-factor. Slot 2 should run multi-sample averaging at x in {10^9..10^12} to tighten empirical confirmation; theoretical extrapolation to x = 10^15, 10^20 via S195's predictor; verify named-exponent corollary at extreme x. **Cross-domain ingredient**: re-uses S195's GUE / random-phase heuristic (Montgomery 1973, Odlyzko 1989); CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md updated to mark this as a complementary algorithmic re-framing of the variance formula. Cites E1.5 (per-query bit-content barrier), E2.1 (spectral / sieve), E3.1 (CCM spectral triple), S195 (variance formula), S196 (Galway frontier closure conditional on random-phase), S202 (unified CCM closure), S224 (Correlation Dichotomy partial-positive template Thread 7 follows). See `experiments/analytic/polylog_approx_pi/{polylog_approx_pi.py, polylog_approx_pi_results.md, polylog_approx_pi_main.csv, main_run.log}`, `archive/sessions/session240_commit_p3_partial_sum_evaluator.md`. | 240 |
